/**
 * @defgroup Foundation_Functional Functional
 * @ingroup Foundation
 * @brief Allocation-free callable utilities for embedded and desktop code.
 *
 * Functional currently exposes one public component:
 * @ref Foundation_Callback "Callback". This is the complete implemented v1
 * surface of the module, not a missing-documentation placeholder. Additional
 * functional utilities should appear here only after they have an implemented,
 * tested, and reviewed public contract.
 *
 * @section FoundationFunctionalHeaders Public Headers
 *
 * | Need | Header |
 * | ---- | ------ |
 * | Entire Foundation library | `#include <Foundation.h>` |
 * | Entire Functional module | `#include <Foundation_Functional.h>` |
 * | Nested module umbrella | `#include <Foundation/Functional.h>` |
 * | Callback only | `#include <Foundation/Functional/Callback.h>` |
 *
 * @section FoundationFunctionalUsage Basic Usage
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * #include <Foundation_Functional.h>
 *
 * int Add(int first, int second) {
 *     return first + second;
 * }
 *
 * Foundation::Functional::Callback<int, int, int> callback;
 * callback.Bind(Add);
 * const int result = callback.Invoke(2, 3);
 * @endcode
 *
 * Callback stores either a free/static function pointer or a non-owning object
 * pointer plus a member-function invoker. It performs no heap allocation and
 * offers `IsBound()` and `Unbind()` for explicit state management.
 *
 * @section FoundationFunctionalContract Current Contract
 *
 * - Bound objects are not owned; they must outlive the binding and every call.
 * - Non-const and const member functions are supported. Const functions may be
 *   bound to const objects.
 * - A callback without arguments uses an empty pack: `Callback<R>` or
 *   `Callback<void>`. `void` is not an argument placeholder.
 * - If `FOUNDATION_EXCEPTIONS` is enabled, invoking an empty callback throws
 *   `std::runtime_error`. Otherwise a non-void callback returns `R{}` and a
 *   void callback performs no operation.
 * - Callback invocation is synchronous and is not internally synchronized.
 *
 * @section FoundationFunctionalExample Runnable Example
 *
 * `Foundation_Functional_Callback` demonstrates free functions, member
 * functions, return values, binding state, and unbinding. See
 * @ref Foundation_Examples "Examples" for build and launch instructions.
 */

/**
 * @namespace Foundation::Functional
 * @ingroup Foundation_Functional
 * @brief Allocation-free callable abstractions.
 */
